error[E0277]: `MyError` cannot absorb an unclosed-delimiter diagnostic for lexer `L`
  --> tests/ui/from_unclosed.rs:11:14
   |
11 |   inner::<L, MyError>();
   |              ^^^^^^^ this error type has no `FromUnclosed` impl
   |
   = help: the trait `FromUnclosed<'_, L>` is not implemented for `MyError`
   = note: one generic impl covers every delimiter pair, user-defined ones included: `impl<'i, L: Lexer<'i>, Lang: ?Sized> FromUnclosed<'i, L, Lang> for MyError { fn from_unclosed<D>(e: Unclosed<D, L::Span, Lang>) -> Self { /* … */ } }`
   = note: pin the span if your error stores it — an opaque `L::Span` has no route to a concrete span type: `L: Lexer<'i, Span = SimpleSpan>`
   = note: match on `Unclosed::name_ref` to discriminate the pair — `"()"`, `"<>"`, `"[]"`, `"{}"` for the built-ins — and keep a catch-all arm: `D` is generic, so no arm set is exhaustive
   = help: the trait `FromUnclosed<'inp, L, Lang>` is implemented for `()`
note: required by a bound in `inner`
